Analyze the following C# class where property validation is required:

public class UserProfile {
    private string _displayName;
    public string DisplayName {
        get => _displayName;
        set => _displayName = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(value) 
            ? throw new ArgumentException("Invalid name") 
            : value.Trim();
    }
}

MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS:
1. Explain the new C# 14 (.NET 10) feature that allows direct access to the compiler-generated backing field without manually declaring an explicit private field '_displayName'.
2. Refactor the property using the contextual keyword 'field' to eliminate the explicit private field.

